.TH DAGONFS 1 "15 November 2026" "DAGonFS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dagonfs, DAGonFS_Launcher \- MPI-distributed, in-memory FUSE file system for workflow scratch data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mpirun \-np
.I P
[\fImpirun-options\fR]
.B dagonfs
[\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-model\fR \fIclient-server\fR|\fIpeer-to-peer\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-d\fR]
[\fB\-\-log\fR]
[\fIroot\fR]
.br
.B DAGonFS_Launcher
[\fIDAGonFS.ini\fR]
[\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-model\fR \fImodel\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-dry-run\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dagonfs
turns a directory into a POSIX namespace whose file contents are spread over the
memory of the processes of an MPI job. It is designed for the scratch data of
scientific workflows, such as those run by DAGonStar. It does not provide durable
storage: unmounting the file system or ending the job discards its contents.
.PP
.B dagonfs
runs on every rank of the job. The deployment model is chosen for each volume when it is created:
.TP
.B client-server
(default) Rank 0 mounts
.I root
and serves every request. Ranks 1 to P\-1 store blocks.
.TP
.B peer-to-peer
Rank
.I r
mounts
.IR root / r .
Every peer serves its own mount and replicates namespace and metadata changes to
the other peers. Data written and closed on one peer can be read on any other.
.PP
A file's content is held by the front end while the file is open. It is
distributed to all ranks in blocks of 128 KiB on
.BR fsync ,
on a flush of a dirty file, and on the last close (close-to-open consistency).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " " \fImodel\fR
.B client-server
(alias
.BR cs )
or
.B peer-to-peer
(alias
.BR p2p ).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Read
.BR dagonfs_model ,
.BR dagonfs_root_dir ,
.B fuse_mode
and
.B enable_logging
from the
.B [DAGonFS_config]
section of an ini file.
.TP
.B \-f
Run FUSE in the foreground (default; required under MPI).
.TP
.B \-d
Foreground, with a trace of every FUSE request.
.TP
.B \-\-log
Verbose logging. The legacy form is a trailing
.B 1
(and
.B 0
to disable it).
.TP
.I root
Mount point (client-server) or parent of the per-rank mount points (peer-to-peer).
It may be omitted when the configuration file sets
.BR dagonfs_root_dir .
Missing directories are created.
.PP
Precedence, from lowest to highest: built-in defaults, the program name, the
configuration file, explicit options. The names
.B DAGonFS_CS.exe
and
.B DAGonFS_P2P.exe
are symbolic links to
.B dagonfs
that select the client-server and peer-to-peer model by default, so legacy
invocations keep working.
.SH LAUNCHER
.B DAGonFS_Launcher
reads a configuration file (default
.BR ./DAGonFS.ini )
and runs
.B mpirun
through
.BR execvp (3),
without a shell. Keys of the
.B [DAGonFS_config]
section:
.BR num_processes " (required), " machinefile ", " mpirun ", " executable ,
.BR dagonfs_model ", " dagonfs_root_dir " (required), " fuse_mode ", " enable_logging .
.B \-\-model
overrides
.BR dagonfs_model ;
.B \-\-dry-run
prints the command instead of running it.
.SH STOPPING A VOLUME
Unmount the front end, for example
.BR "fusermount3 \-u" " " \fIroot\fR,
or any one peer's mount point in peer-to-peer mode. The other ranks then shut down
by themselves. Killing the MPI job instead leaves stale mount points, which must be
removed with
.BR "fusermount3 \-u" .
.SH POSIX OPERATIONS
Supported: creation, lookup and removal of files and directories,
.BR rename (2)
(including
.BR RENAME_NOREPLACE ),
hard and symbolic links, FIFOs
.RB ( mkfifo (3)),
Unix-domain sockets and device nodes
.RB ( mknod (2);
devices need privilege), reads and writes at any offset,
.BR mmap (2),
truncation,
.BR chmod ,
.BR chown ,
.BR utimensat ,
extended attributes,
.BR statfs ,
.BR fsync ,
.BR posix_fallocate (3)
and
.BR fallocate (2)
(allocate,
.BR FALLOC_FL_KEEP_SIZE ,
.BR FALLOC_FL_PUNCH_HOLE ,
.BR FALLOC_FL_ZERO_RANGE ),
.BR lseek (2)
with
.B SEEK_DATA
and
.BR SEEK_HOLE ,
.BR copy_file_range (2),
.BR poll (2),
and directory listing with attributes (readdirplus).
.PP
Advisory locks are cluster-wide: POSIX record locks
.RB ( fcntl (2)
.BR F_GETLK ,
.BR F_SETLK ,
.BR F_SETLKW ,
and
.BR lockf (3))
and
.BR flock (2)
locks exclude processes on every node of the volume. A waiting request does not block the file system; it fails with
.B EDEADLK
when it would deadlock and with
.B EINTR
when a signal interrupts it. Closing a descriptor releases the process's record locks on the file after its data have been written back. The lock table is held by rank 0; other peers reach it through MPI.
.PP
.BR ioctl (2)
fails with
.BR ENOTTY .
.B O_TMPFILE
fails with
.BR EOPNOTSUPP ,
POSIX ACLs with
.BR ENOTSUP ,
and the
.B fallocate
modes collapse, insert and unshare with
.BR EOPNOTSUPP .
.SH ENVIRONMENT AND REQUIREMENTS
Every node needs
.BR /dev/fuse ,
a set-uid
.B fusermount3
and libfuse 3. A peer-to-peer volume requires an MPI library providing
.BR MPI_THREAD_MULTIPLE .
All ranks must run the same binary on the same architecture.
.PP
.B dagonfs
uses point-to-point MPI messages only. With Open MPI it disables the HCOLL
collective component (it sets
.B OMPI_MCA_coll_hcoll_enable=0
unless the environment sets it), whose teardown could deadlock
.BR MPI_Finalize .
.PP
Applications may use MPI-IO on a mounted volume: both Open MPI implementations
(OMPIO and ROMIO) are tested, including collective I/O, data sieving under
byte-range locks, atomic mode and the shared file pointer.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the volume was unmounted normally; non-zero when it could not be mounted.
Startup errors are reported on standard error with the rank number.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mpirun \-np 4 dagonfs \-\-model client\-server \-f /tmp/dagonfs
mpirun \-np 4 dagonfs \-\-model peer\-to\-peer \-f /tmp/dagonfs   # /tmp/dagonfs/0 ... /3
mpirun \-np 4 dagonfs \-\-config DAGonFS.ini
DAGonFS_Launcher \-\-model peer\-to\-peer \-\-dry\-run
fusermount3 \-u /tmp/dagonfs
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fusermount3 (1),
.BR mpirun (1).
The project documentation (architecture, protocol, configuration, performance,
DAGonStar integration) is installed under
.BR share/doc/DAGonFS
and maintained in the
.B docs
directory of the source tree.
